1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
You... weren't invited, were you?

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Hey, Karasuno's number 10!

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,000
You little... what the hell do you think you're doing, Hinata?

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Damn it!

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Hinata, there's a difference between being a go-getter and a loose cannon.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,000
I'm not here because I think this will help me more than our practice will.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,000
This camp has so many strong players. I want to be a part of it.

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Without the play of your personal setter, Kageyama, I don't see you as being worth anything.

9
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,000
If you don't like being a ball boy, you're welcome to go home at any time.

10
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,000
I'm very sorry for interrupting practice.

11
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
I'm a first-year from Karasuno High School! Shouyo Hinata!

12
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,000
I'm 164 centimeters tall!

13
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
My position is ball boy! Thank you for having me!

14
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,000
zar premium

15
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,000
swimming

16
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
notice

17
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,000
however

18
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,000
I'm so happy for enhancing music

19
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
I'm Horror

20
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,000
I'm hard

21
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:13,880
I can hear

22
00:01:13,880 --> 00:01:15,000
I have to play

23
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:44,980
I'll see you next time.

24
00:01:45,000 --> 00:02:14,980
See you next time.

25
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:44,980
See you next time.

26
00:02:44,980 --> 00:02:47,600
You're doing reps you need to visualize an actual game.

27
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:48,320
Yes, sir!

28
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:50,720
All right, let me hear you newbies!

29
00:02:50,720 --> 00:02:52,080
Now, if you'll excuse me, Specs.

30
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:53,740
Here I go!

31
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:55,400
I'm gonna head out for a bit.

32
00:02:55,860 --> 00:02:57,320
You're going to Yamagata, right?

33
00:02:57,460 --> 00:02:57,720
One more!

34
00:02:58,020 --> 00:03:00,760
Yeah, I need to go see an old friend of mine from college.

35
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:04,600
I'm gonna stop by Shira Torizawa too, but try not to get in the way of practice.

36
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:05,360
Bring it on!

37
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:10,560
I'll save my lecture for Hinata until right after the two of us get back tomorrow.

38
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:14,120
I asked Tatsun to come in and help you.

39
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:16,300
It shouldn't take him much longer to get here.

40
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:18,660
I appreciate that, thanks.

41
00:03:19,060 --> 00:03:22,340
That reminds me, there was some talk about your dad coming to a practice?

42
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:24,520
Uh, yeah?

43
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:31,320
The old man kind of got himself sick again the other day, so he's back in the hospital

44
00:03:31,320 --> 00:03:31,820
for now.

45
00:03:32,820 --> 00:03:34,860
Oh, I'm sorry to hear that.

46
00:03:35,380 --> 00:03:36,240
No, it's okay.

47
00:03:36,340 --> 00:03:37,660
It's not serious or anything.

48
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:39,480
I'm gonna head out now.

49
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:41,380
All right, take care.

50
00:03:44,060 --> 00:03:48,220
Normally, you kids are playing against each other in qualifying matches.

51
00:03:48,860 --> 00:03:52,560
However, while you're in this gym, you're not opponents any longer.

52
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:57,540
Just the fact that you're doing something different will be a key stimulus.

53
00:03:58,220 --> 00:04:01,060
Take whatever you can from each other and make each other better.

54
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:02,580
That is all.

55
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:04,380
Thank you, sir.

56
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:07,180
Let's see.

57
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:08,980
First, yep, that's right.

58
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:09,800
Passing drills.

59
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:12,260
Now start off by learning your partner's name.

60
00:04:12,860 --> 00:04:15,560
Try and pair with someone who's on a different skill level than you.

61
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:17,580
Come on, guys.

62
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:18,380
Let's go.

63
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:22,200
Wow, he really is the odd man out.

64
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:24,820
But he's one of Karasuno's starting players.

65
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:27,340
Um, hey there.

66
00:04:27,740 --> 00:04:29,880
We heard that you're the ball boy from Karasuno.

67
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:31,580
That's right!

68
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:35,480
It's Karasuno's number 10.

69
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:39,760
Um, we're second-string first-years from Shiratorizawa.

70
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:43,280
We're just here to help out with the training camp, so it's nice to work with you.

71
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:43,620
Uh-huh!

72
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:44,140
Same!

73
00:04:44,140 --> 00:05:00,640
Man, two meters is really tall.

74
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:03,480
I wonder what everything looks like from way up there.

75
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:09,040
That guy didn't start playing until high school, and he's already been chosen for special training?

76
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:10,860
Yeah.

77
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:13,140
He'll be learning some of the basics, I guess.

78
00:05:13,640 --> 00:05:15,600
Turn them so the inside's facing off.

79
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:18,440
All right, next, spiking drills.

80
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:18,840
Huh?

81
00:05:19,780 --> 00:05:20,340
Hey!

82
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:22,840
You're going the wrong direction, ball boy.

83
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:29,800
Sorry, sir!

84
00:05:30,060 --> 00:05:30,720
My mistake!

85
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:36,160
Just place the ball.

86
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:37,240
Just place the ball.

87
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:42,020
So how was my set?

88
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:45,000
Fine, I guess.

89
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:47,100
Come on, give me more than that!

90
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:49,740
That's Kogunagawa from Date Tech.

91
00:05:50,180 --> 00:05:51,520
His technical skills aren't there.

92
00:05:51,820 --> 00:05:52,820
Or there yet, anyway.

93
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:54,080
But he's still getting taller.

94
00:05:54,740 --> 00:05:55,660
I like it.

95
00:05:55,760 --> 00:05:56,700
A giant setter.

96
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:04,160
Nice kill!

97
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:06,500
Was that one a little too high for you?

98
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,620
Yeah, a little bit.

99
00:06:09,060 --> 00:06:10,120
Cool, I can fix it.

100
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:15,000
Shota Yura, a third year from Shira Torizawa's middle school division.

101
00:06:15,260 --> 00:06:18,500
Looks like he's got no problems communicating with any of the older players.

102
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:20,440
And he's got some technique, too.

103
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:23,940
Nice one!

104
00:06:25,060 --> 00:06:26,460
Oh, crap!

105
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:30,720
Hey, someone could get hurt!

106
00:06:31,060 --> 00:06:32,720
Do your job, ball boy!

107
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:33,400
Yes, sir!

108
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:34,720
Use your eyes, kid!

109
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:35,180
Yes, sir!

110
00:06:35,180 --> 00:06:38,800
I think this dude's getting yelled at even more than we are.

111
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:40,900
This doesn't make sense.

112
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:43,360
I wonder why Coach Washijo let him stick around.

113
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:46,960
I'd say if he's not here to practice, he should just be forced to go home.

114
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:50,060
The coach generally isn't interested in smaller players anyway.

115
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:51,220
So I hear.

116
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,760
It really is a shame to waste him, though.

117
00:06:54,220 --> 00:06:57,240
If he were on my team, I'd probably train him to be a wing spiker.

118
00:06:57,240 --> 00:07:00,380
Karasuno did take the Spring Nationals from them this year.

119
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:00,900
You got it!

120
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:02,640
Maybe this is his way of getting revenge.

121
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:03,020
Here he comes!

122
00:07:03,360 --> 00:07:05,380
Ah, he'd never do anything like that.

123
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:11,600
Nice kill!

124
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:24,960
I'm starving.

125
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:29,580
Come on, guys.

126
00:07:29,660 --> 00:07:30,340
Let's go home.

127
00:07:30,340 --> 00:07:32,340
Let's go home.

128
00:07:32,340 --> 00:07:32,520
Yeah.

129
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:36,680
That little runt.

130
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:41,080
In middle school, he had newbie written all over him, but not anymore.

131
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:44,060
He must have spent a lot of time on the court.

132
00:07:44,060 --> 00:07:56,820
Damn it.

133
00:07:57,320 --> 00:07:58,760
Jump serves are really hard.

134
00:08:01,240 --> 00:08:05,420
Come to think of it, this is the first time I've ever just been a ball boy.

135
00:08:06,100 --> 00:08:10,680
With the ladies' team and the girls' team at my middle school, they all let me practice with them.

136
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:13,600
What have you been wasting your time on?

137
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:14,980
For the last three years!

138
00:08:31,240 --> 00:08:32,860
We'll beat you next time.

139
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:39,340
I'll see you from the top.

140
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:46,960
I can't stop!

141
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:49,280
I can't!

142
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:55,320
Hinata.

143
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:58,460
Could you please get yourself ready to leave?

144
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:03,120
We don't get an excused absence like his majesty does for his intensive.

145
00:09:03,820 --> 00:09:05,860
You and I still have to go into school tomorrow.

146
00:09:05,860 --> 00:09:06,860
Tsukishima!

147
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:07,780
Tsukishima!

148
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:09,780
I...

149
00:09:09,780 --> 00:09:10,460
I...

150
00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:12,180
I'm sorry for-

151
00:09:12,180 --> 00:09:14,020
Yeah, could you not apologize to me?

152
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:17,720
It's not like you being an impulsive dumbass is new or anything.

153
00:09:18,080 --> 00:09:18,840
Is it killing you?

154
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:20,260
You barely got to touch the ball.

155
00:09:20,620 --> 00:09:21,860
You did it to yourself.

156
00:09:22,340 --> 00:09:23,480
Are you ready to give up?

157
00:09:23,580 --> 00:09:24,880
Are you gonna cry and quit?

158
00:09:25,220 --> 00:09:27,620
You just be the best ball boy you can be.

159
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:30,140
There are five precious days before nationals.

160
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:31,240
Don't waste them.

161
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:33,360
Wow.

162
00:09:33,980 --> 00:09:35,720
Can you believe that Hinata kid?

163
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:38,840
He had a ball in his hand right up to the very last second.

164
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:42,500
Still, it was a surprise to have him crash the camp.

165
00:09:42,500 --> 00:09:47,320
I have nothing against kids who are a little reckless.

166
00:09:48,180 --> 00:09:56,540
That said, I don't care how hard the kid works or how much determination he shows off while he's out there or how much grit he's got.

167
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:59,120
I'm not going to let him practice with the others.

168
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:06,480
Hey, I'm here to get this week's issue of Jump Back!

169
00:10:07,480 --> 00:10:12,020
I'm still on Removes Unnecessary Hair and Leaves Skin Feeling Silky Smooth.

170
00:10:12,020 --> 00:10:14,800
Could you read the actual manga instead of the ads?

171
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:18,740
Oh, and hey, you're going to the first year's training camp tomorrow.

172
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:20,720
Right, Ishiwaka?

173
00:10:22,660 --> 00:10:23,360
That's right.

174
00:10:42,020 --> 00:10:51,460
So, did you honestly think you could just show up there and they'd let you practice with them?

175
00:10:51,460 --> 00:11:00,720
Everyone's so far ahead of me.

176
00:11:01,340 --> 00:11:03,320
I figured I had to catch up somehow.

177
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:05,580
I mean, he's not wrong.

178
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:08,040
Not smart, but not wrong.

179
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:13,880
Even if that's true, it doesn't make it okay for you to cause trouble for everyone.

180
00:11:14,560 --> 00:11:15,240
Yes, sir.

181
00:11:15,240 --> 00:11:25,120
So, you're saying Coach Washijo says it doesn't make any difference whatsoever whether Hinata stays here or not?

182
00:11:25,760 --> 00:11:28,880
Well, I guess that's true.

183
00:11:30,060 --> 00:11:33,820
So, you proudly declared yourself the ball boy.

184
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:37,120
Yes, sir.

185
00:11:37,120 --> 00:11:43,620
Well, you got yourself into this mess.

186
00:11:44,140 --> 00:11:45,580
You'd better not regret it.

187
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:48,980
Figure out what you can do there that you can't do anywhere else.

188
00:11:50,740 --> 00:11:53,360
Meanwhile, don't underestimate your new job.

189
00:11:53,360 --> 00:12:11,460
He who wishes to climb the ladder must start out at the bottom.

190
00:12:13,860 --> 00:12:18,380
When you're going to do something, it's important to be sure to follow the proper steps.

191
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:20,640
And that's all.

192
00:12:21,220 --> 00:12:22,920
Do you have anything you'd like to say, Hinata?

193
00:12:22,920 --> 00:12:26,840
That's all, sir.

194
00:12:28,220 --> 00:12:29,340
Please excuse me.

195
00:12:35,300 --> 00:12:37,320
One lecture after another, eh?

196
00:12:38,860 --> 00:12:40,100
Did she get you yet?

197
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:43,980
First thing this morning.

198
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:46,240
How many times, kid?

199
00:12:46,460 --> 00:12:49,740
You have to think about how your actions will affect other people.

200
00:12:50,020 --> 00:12:51,420
Yeah, good going, Hinata.

201
00:12:51,740 --> 00:12:52,180
Suga!

202
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:53,180
Shutting up.

203
00:12:53,180 --> 00:13:02,900
I mean, well, you do suck at volleyball, so going to that camp and learning a killer move

204
00:13:02,900 --> 00:13:03,820
or two might help.

205
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:07,600
You don't really get a chance to play with guys from other teams every day, you know.

206
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:10,440
But hey, you don't have to be in such a hurry.

207
00:13:10,440 --> 00:13:11,680
Now get lost.

208
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:16,440
I'm sorry.

209
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:19,100
Hinata, my man!

210
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:20,720
How's the training camp going?

211
00:13:20,720 --> 00:13:24,060
That two-meter guy's playing there and he's super tall!

212
00:13:24,060 --> 00:13:24,880
He's there too?

213
00:13:25,100 --> 00:13:26,440
What's his name, Manzawa?

214
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:27,640
It's Yakazawa.

215
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:41,860
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight.

216
00:13:41,860 --> 00:13:44,860
Hey, Hinata, do you think you could take care of the drinks again?

217
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:46,060
You got it!

218
00:13:46,060 --> 00:13:48,860
Today, we'll be doing serving and spiking drills.

219
00:13:49,280 --> 00:13:50,920
After that, we'll have a scrimmage.

220
00:13:51,280 --> 00:13:51,940
Yes, sir!

221
00:13:51,940 --> 00:13:59,220
Hey, wake up, ball boy!

222
00:13:59,460 --> 00:14:00,080
Sorry, sir!

223
00:14:05,540 --> 00:14:07,760
God, a perfect line shot!

224
00:14:08,700 --> 00:14:09,180
Whoa!

225
00:14:09,460 --> 00:14:10,420
That's a nice kill.

226
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:11,740
Doski!

227
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:12,520
Yes, sir?

228
00:14:12,620 --> 00:14:14,360
The way you position your body...

229
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:14,760
Yes, sir?

230
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:15,800
...it makes you more predictable.

231
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:22,160
Nice kill, man!

232
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:25,020
Bring it, Yakazawa!

233
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:36,600
What the heck was that?

234
00:14:37,020 --> 00:14:38,040
It was so cool!

235
00:14:38,500 --> 00:14:40,020
And that perfect line shot!

236
00:14:40,540 --> 00:14:41,220
Do it again!

237
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:44,140
All right, Nyx, line up for a game!

238
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:45,260
Yes, sir!

239
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:47,580
Hinata, get the jerseys!

240
00:14:47,860 --> 00:14:48,440
Oh, right!

241
00:14:50,980 --> 00:14:51,340
Nagamatsu!

242
00:14:53,340 --> 00:14:54,220
Nice receive!

243
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:56,380
Left side!

244
00:14:57,180 --> 00:14:58,740
So I hear that Nagamatsu guy.

245
00:14:58,960 --> 00:15:00,180
He's a middle school third year.

246
00:15:00,540 --> 00:15:02,220
He's going to be coming to our school.

247
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:04,420
Dang, he's going to be on our team?

248
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:07,860
Hey, guys!

249
00:15:08,340 --> 00:15:08,580
Huh?

250
00:15:09,480 --> 00:15:10,780
Well, here they are.

251
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:17,480
Hello!

252
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:17,740
Hello!

253
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:17,880
Hello!

254
00:15:30,140 --> 00:15:30,680
Ugh!

255
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:30,740
So, we're quite fortunate today.

256
00:15:31,340 --> 00:15:34,280
A few of Shira Torizawa's third years and alums are here.

257
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:36,780
They've agreed to have a practice match with you boys.

258
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:39,040
Yay!

259
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:40,040
Hey.

260
00:15:40,040 --> 00:15:41,040
Seriously?

261
00:15:41,040 --> 00:15:42,040
Come on.

262
00:15:42,040 --> 00:15:43,040
Ugh.

263
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:44,040
Wow!

264
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:45,040
It's Ushiwaka!

265
00:15:45,040 --> 00:15:46,040
It really is him.

266
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:49,040
Ushiwaka's right there.

267
00:15:49,040 --> 00:15:52,040
A practice match with Ushiwaka!

268
00:15:52,040 --> 00:15:56,040
